### 2.2 Queue Architecture

```
                    ┌─────────────────────┐
                    │   Celery Beat        │
                    │   (Scheduler)        │
                    └──────────┬──────────┘
                               │
    ┌──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┐
    │                          │                          │
    ▼                          ▼                          ▼
┌───────────┐          ┌──────────────┐          ┌──────────────┐
│  Email    │          │  Social       │          │  Analytics   │
│  Queue    │          │  Queue        │          │  Queue       │
│ (high)    │          │  (medium)     │          │  (low)       │
└─────┬─────┘          └──────┬───────┘          └──────┬───────┘
      │                       │                         │
      ▼                       ▼                         ▼
┌─────────────┐        ┌─────────────┐          ┌─────────────┐
│ Email Worker│        │ Social      │          │ Analytics   │
│ (5-10 pods) │        │ Worker      │          │ Worker      │
│             │        │ (3-5 pods)  │          │ (2-3 pods)  │
└─────────────┘        └─────────────┘          └─────────────┘

Queue Priorities:
  high:     Campaign sends, transactional emails
  medium:   Social publishing, AI content generation
  low:      Analytics sync, data aggregation, cleanup tasks

Priority via separate Celery queues (not routing keys):
  CELERY_TASK_QUEUES = {
      'high':   {'exchange': 'high',   'routing_key': 'high'},
      'medium': {'exchange': 'medium', 'routing_key': 'medium'},
      'low':    {'exchange': 'low',    'routing_key': 'low'},
  }
```

### 2.3 Data Flow — Email Campaign Send

```
User clicks "Send Campaign"
  → View validates + creates CampaignTask record
  → Celery task enqueued on 'high' queue
  → Email Worker picks up task
  → Worker resolves recipients (pagination, 500/batch)
  → For each batch:
      → Render email template with context
      → Inject tracking pixel (1x1 transparent GIF with unique ID)
      → Wrap links with click-tracking redirect
      → Send via SMTP/GmailAPI/GraphAPI (per sender config)
      → Record SentEvent per recipient
  → On delivery failure:
      → Record BounceEvent
      → Update campaign stats
      → Retry with exponential backoff (max 3)
  → After all batches:
      → Mark campaign as 'sent'
      → Trigger analytics aggregation
```

### 2.4 Data Flow — AI Email Reply

```
Incoming Email (webhook/poll)
  → Gmail API push notification OR Celery Beat poll
  → Ingest email → store as InboundEmail
  → Enqueue AI processing task (medium queue)
  → AI Agent Worker:
      1. Summarize email content
      2. Detect intent (question, complaint, sales, support)
      3. Detect urgency (low/medium/high/critical)
      4. Fetch conversation history from AI memory
      5. Generate contextual reply via AI provider
      6. Store as DraftReply (status: needs_review)
  → Notify user via WebSocket + in-app notification
  → User reviews draft in dashboard
  → User edits (optional) → approves
  → Reply saved to Gmail drafts via Gmail Draft API
  → User sends from Gmail interface OR platform sends via SMTP
```

